00:02:58.510 --> 00:03:00.220
- What has been the
hardest challenge so far

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:02.050
in juggling between being a K-pop star

00:03:02.050 --> 00:03:03.730
and also keeping yourself grounded?

00:03:03.730 --> 00:03:06.880
How do you cope with both mental
and physical health stress?

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:09.140
- I like my job, I like what I do,

00:03:09.140 --> 00:03:11.300
and I think when I'm really
really immersed in it,

00:03:11.300 --> 00:03:13.410
you just kinda forget
everything around you,

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:15.510
so it's always good to remember to get up,

00:03:15.530 --> 00:03:17.410
walk around, eat something.

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:20.340
Mental health is a very,
very big part of life.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.010
I think people don't tend to think about

00:03:22.010 --> 00:03:24.720
definitely taking the time
out to have some alone time,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.350
and also sharing your problems and

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:30.280
being able to talk about
it, be vulnerable to,

00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:31.213
I guess, people around you.

00:03:31.213 --> 00:03:33.224
I think people are sometimes
scared to share because

00:03:33.224 --> 00:03:34.490
they don't want to be judged.

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:36.154
- And you do have a lot of
supportive people in your life.

00:03:36.154 --> 00:03:36.987
- Yes, yes.

00:03:36.987 --> 00:03:37.820
- That's great.

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:38.653
Who's your personal hero?

00:03:38.653 --> 00:03:39.486
- My sister.

00:03:39.486 --> 00:03:41.792
Jackie is the complete opposite
of me, and I look up to her.

00:03:41.792 --> 00:03:42.625
- I feel like you guys are,

00:03:42.625 --> 00:03:44.183
you guys have similar personalities.

00:03:44.183 --> 00:03:46.370
You guys are both outgoing,
both really friendly.

00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.360
- She made me become outgoing.

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.930
My sister's really taught
me how to be in touch with

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:52.980
my emotions and making sure

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:55.440
having emotions is not
something to be ashamed of.

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:57.880
- How do you think male K-pop idols

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:59.480
feel about doing so much skinship

00:03:59.480 --> 00:04:02.380
since there's so much fragile
masculinity in the States?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:04.660
And masculinity is important to men.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.120
- Masculinity and femininity
are on a spectrum.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.230
You can be any part on that spectrum.

00:04:10.230 --> 00:04:12.180
Honestly, if you're
close to that person and

00:04:12.180 --> 00:04:14.615
they consent to that touching, go ahead.

00:04:14.615 --> 00:04:15.448
- Yeah.

00:04:15.448 --> 00:04:17.305
I'm very touchy with my bros.

00:04:17.305 --> 00:04:18.860
I'm really touchy.

00:04:18.860 --> 00:04:20.860
- With girls, too, girls
link arms all the time.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:22.030
I'm so scared of linking arms.

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:24.150
I do not consent to people
linking arms with me.

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.870
There's only, like, a couple
people that I got used to it.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:28.170
Krystal is one of them, my member.

00:04:28.170 --> 00:04:30.426
Oh my gosh, when she
links arms, I'm just like

00:04:30.426 --> 00:04:31.694
(grunts)

00:04:31.694 --> 00:04:33.454
- But you guys have been
together for nine years.

00:04:33.454 --> 00:04:34.340
- I don't know, it's just, like,

00:04:34.340 --> 00:04:36.084
you're in my armpit area,
and it's just like...

00:04:36.084 --> 00:04:36.917
(laughter)

00:04:36.917 --> 00:04:38.073
- Armpit area!

00:04:38.073 --> 00:04:40.534
So when you see Amber
next time, link your arm.

00:04:40.534 --> 00:04:41.680
(laughs)

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:42.513
Just link.

00:04:42.513 --> 00:04:44.630
- What was it like in the
Korean music industry,

00:04:44.630 --> 00:04:47.200
being a female idol, to not prescribe

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:49.320
to "typical" gender roles
and beauty standards?

00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:51.310
What types of criticism and
support did you experience?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:52.143
- (clears throat)

00:04:52.143 --> 00:04:53.260
Sorry, wow.

00:04:53.260 --> 00:04:55.010
This is still burning hot,
god, this doesn't go away.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:56.535
- You're just refusing
to drink that water.

00:04:56.535 --> 00:04:57.368
- Oh.

00:04:57.368 --> 00:04:58.201
(laughter)

00:04:58.201 --> 00:05:01.170
Because K-pop has now
become so international,

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:02.880
once you kinda put yourself out there,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:04.720
you're prone to just getting criticism.

00:05:04.720 --> 00:05:06.470
Definitely, there's a
huge amount of support,

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:08.410
but definitely on the uglier side,

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:10.900
something so simple as, like,
if I wanted to go work out,

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.940
like, "oh my gosh, a girl,
you can't have muscles".

00:05:12.940 --> 00:05:14.910
Things like that happens every day and

00:05:14.910 --> 00:05:16.530
it's something that I've gotten used to.

00:05:16.530 --> 00:05:19.250
Hopefully through what I do,

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.870
I can slowly open someone else's mind.

00:05:21.870 --> 00:05:23.464
Girls, if you wanna go
work out, go work out,

00:05:23.464 --> 00:05:24.870
go get those muscles.

00:05:24.870 --> 00:05:26.740
When I see comments on my Instagram and

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:28.277
on my social media,
they're always just like,

00:05:28.277 --> 00:05:31.895
"thank you so much for
representing the tomboy crew".

00:05:31.895 --> 00:05:33.840
I appreciate all that support.

00:05:33.840 --> 00:05:36.300
- How do you find out you
were allergic to mangoes?

00:05:36.300 --> 00:05:37.500
You're allergic to mangoes!?

00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:38.333
- Yes.

00:05:38.436 --> 00:05:39.800
- (groans) Oh my god, Amber, no.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:42.593
- So I can eat mangoes,
I just can't touch it.

00:05:42.612 --> 00:05:43.445
- What?

00:05:43.445 --> 00:05:44.278
- Yeah.

00:05:44.278 --> 00:05:45.940
Literally if I have a
mango and I wanna eat it,

00:05:45.940 --> 00:05:47.970
I have to wear gloves so
that the juice doesn't

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:48.803
touch my skin.

00:05:48.803 --> 00:05:50.180
I remember one time I was eating a mango,

00:05:50.180 --> 00:05:51.453
and I went like this.

00:05:51.453 --> 00:05:52.286
- With the juice.

00:05:52.286 --> 00:05:53.119
- With the juice.

00:05:53.119 --> 00:05:54.630
And my ear got a rash.

00:05:54.630 --> 00:05:55.463
I can eat it though.

00:05:55.463 --> 00:05:56.750
- But it touches your lips
when you're eating it.

00:05:56.750 --> 00:05:57.850
Nothing but the teeth.

00:05:58.550 --> 00:05:59.640
- This is me eating mangoes.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:00.473
- Do you like shrimps?

00:06:00.473 --> 00:06:01.306
- I love shrimp.

00:06:01.306 --> 00:06:02.232
- I can't eat shrimp,
I'm allergic to shrimps.

00:06:02.232 --> 00:06:03.065
- (gasps)

00:06:03.065 --> 00:06:04.172
- When I eat it, I get hives,

00:06:04.172 --> 00:06:05.980
and I was like, "my life is over".

00:06:05.980 --> 00:06:07.111
- Can you eat lobster?

00:06:07.111 --> 00:06:08.252
- I can eat lobster.

00:06:08.252 --> 00:06:09.085
- Okay, that's fine.

00:06:09.085 --> 00:06:09.918
- It's just shrimp.

00:06:09.918 --> 00:06:10.751
- Okay, okay, good.

00:06:10.751 --> 00:06:13.201
- What are your personal
thoughts on LGBT people,

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:14.920
especially in the K-pop industry?

00:06:14.920 --> 00:06:16.230
- My good friend Marshall,

00:06:16.230 --> 00:06:18.270
he's gay and he's also
in the K-pop industry.

00:06:18.270 --> 00:06:19.610
It's very, very progressive,

00:06:19.610 --> 00:06:21.860
and I really thank them for their bravery.

00:06:21.860 --> 00:06:22.830
Times are changing right now.

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.820
- Yeah. For the good. For the better.

00:06:24.820 --> 00:06:26.743
- LGBT community, just do you,

00:06:26.743 --> 00:06:29.505
stay strong, we got people
out here supporting you.

00:06:29.505 --> 00:06:32.143
- Very, very good to see
that people are supportive.

00:06:32.143 --> 00:06:33.810
Time's are changing for the better.

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:36.627
Should we expect any comebacks from f(x)?

00:06:36.830 --> 00:06:38.440
- Me and the members are
always talking about it.

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:39.560
Right now I think we're
just taking time to

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:40.840
do our own careers at the moment.

00:06:40.840 --> 00:06:42.310
Luna's putting out her own single.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:44.520
Krystal's doing acting,
Victoria's doing acting.

00:06:44.520 --> 00:06:46.420
We're all just kinda
doing our thing right now.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.364
Until the right time comes, right?

00:06:48.364 --> 00:06:51.060
Thank you guys so much for
waiting and being supportive.

00:06:51.060 --> 00:06:51.943
I have a mix tape out.

00:06:51.943 --> 00:06:53.860
Yeah, it's for free too,

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:57.110
so you can go watch that
on my YouTube channel,

00:06:57.110 --> 00:06:58.370
or on SoundCloud.

00:06:58.370 --> 00:06:59.203
Go listen to it.

00:06:59.380 --> 00:07:00.213
Thank you, Evan.

00:07:00.213 --> 00:07:01.503
I'm like, really sweaty.

00:07:01.620 --> 00:07:04.060
People don't know, but my back
